<!-- ==================== 1. Introduction of Design ==================== -->
<section id="sec-intro" class="wetlab-animate">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div class="section-icon">
      <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i>
    </div>
    <div class="section-heading-text">
      <h2 data-text-en="Introduction of Design" data-text-zh="设计概述">Introduction of Design</h2>
      <div class="section-heading-bar"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="drop-cap" data-text-en="Polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons (PAHs) are ubiquitous persistent organic pollutants in urban soil and water environments, mainly derived from vehicle exhaust, asphalt aging, cooking fumes and fossil fuel combustion. As the simplest and most frequently detected low-molecular-weight PAH, naphthalene poses carcinogenic and teratogenic risks under long-term low-dose exposure. According to Chinese national standard GB 36600-2018, strict risk screening values are defined for soil naphthalene contamination. However, conventional HPLC detection requires complicated pretreatment, high cost and laboratory dependence, making rapid on-site screening impossible."
     data-text-zh="多环芳烃（PAHs）是城市土壤与水环境中普遍存在的持久性有机污染物，主要来源于机动车尾气、沥青老化、烹饪油烟及化石燃料燃烧。萘作为结构最简单、检出频率最高的低分子量PAH，长期低剂量暴露具有致癌和致畸风险。根据中国国家标准GB 36600‑2018，土壤萘污染已设有严格的风险筛查值。然而，传统HPLC检测前处理复杂、成本高且依赖实验室，难以实现现场快速筛查。">
    Polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons (PAHs) are ubiquitous persistent organic pollutants in urban soil and water environments, mainly derived from vehicle exhaust, asphalt aging, cooking fumes and fossil fuel combustion. As the simplest and most frequently detected low-molecular-weight PAH, naphthalene poses carcinogenic and teratogenic risks under long-term low-dose exposure. According to Chinese national standard GB 36600-2018, strict risk screening values are defined for soil naphthalene contamination. However, conventional HPLC detection requires complicated pretreatment, high cost and laboratory dependence, making rapid on-site screening impossible.
  </p>

  <p data-text-en="In this project, we constructed a dual-strain co-culture biosensing system based on the native naphthalene degradation pathway and NahR-Psal sensing pathway. The engineered degrader strain metabolizes naphthalene into salicylic acid, while the sensor strain recognizes salicylic acid and triggers eGFP fluorescence expression. The normalized fluorescence intensity (FL/OD₆₀₀) can quantitatively reflect environmental naphthalene concentration."
     data-text-zh="在本项目中，我们基于天然萘降解通路与NahR‑Psal感应通路，构建了一套双菌共培养生物传感系统。工程化降解菌株将萘代谢为水杨酸，传感菌株识别水杨酸并触发eGFP荧光表达；归一化荧光强度（FL/OD₆₀₀）可定量反映环境萘浓度。">
    In this project, we constructed a <strong>dual-strain co-culture biosensing system</strong> based on the native naphthalene degradation pathway and NahR-Psal sensing pathway. The engineered degrader strain metabolizes naphthalene into salicylic acid, while the sensor strain recognizes salicylic acid and triggers eGFP fluorescence expression. The normalized fluorescence intensity (FL/OD₆₀₀) can quantitatively reflect environmental naphthalene concentration.
  </p>

  <p data-text-en="The wild-type system suffers from low sensitivity, weak signal output and insufficient degradation efficiency. Therefore, we performed systematic optimization from five dimensions: bidirectional promoter engineering, NahR saturation mutagenesis, degradation promoter replacement, culture condition optimization, and dual-strain system adaptation. Our iterative modifications greatly improved sensitivity, response speed and detection limit, realizing a low-cost and high-performance whole-cell biosensor for environmental PAH screening."
     data-text-zh="野生型系统存在灵敏度低、信号输出弱、降解效率不足等问题。为此，我们从五个维度对系统进行了系统性优化：双向启动子改造、NahR饱和突变、降解启动子替换、培养条件优化以及双菌系统适配。经过多轮迭代改造，系统的灵敏度、响应速度与检测限均大幅提升，最终实现了一款低成本、高性能的环境PAHs全细胞生物传感器。">
    The wild-type system suffers from low sensitivity, weak signal output and insufficient degradation efficiency. Therefore, we performed systematic optimization from five dimensions: <strong>bidirectional promoter engineering, NahR saturation mutagenesis, degradation promoter replacement, culture condition optimization, and dual-strain system adaptation</strong>. Our iterative modifications greatly improved sensitivity, response speed and detection limit, realizing a low-cost and high-performance whole-cell biosensor for environmental PAH screening.
  </p>
</section>

<!-- ==================== 2. Wild-Type System Design and Deficiency Analysis ==================== -->
<section id="sec-wildtype" class="wetlab-animate">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div class="section-icon">
      <i class="fa-solid fa-bacterium"></i>
    </div>
    <div class="section-heading-text">
      <h2 data-text-en="Wild-Type System Design &amp; Deficiency Analysis" data-text-zh="野生型系统设计与缺陷分析">Wild-Type System Design &amp; Deficiency Analysis</h2>
      <div class="section-heading-bar"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p data-text-en="The original pathway is derived from Pseudomonas putida G7, which contains the native NahR-Psal-Pr bidirectional regulatory pathway and complete naphthalene degradation gene cluster. In wild-type strains, NahR recognizes salicylic acid and activates the Psal promoter to drive reporter expression, while the nah gene cluster catalyzes naphthalene-to-salicylate conversion."
     data-text-zh="原始通路来源于恶臭假单胞菌（Pseudomonas putida）G7菌株，其中含有天然的NahR‑Psal‑Pr双向调控通路以及完整的萘降解基因簇。在野生型菌株中，NahR识别水杨酸并激活Psal启动子驱动报告基因表达，而nah基因簇则负责催化萘向水杨酸的转化。">
    The original pathway is derived from <em>Pseudomonas putida</em> G7, which contains the native NahR-Psal-Pr bidirectional regulatory pathway and complete naphthalene degradation gene cluster. In wild-type strains, NahR recognizes salicylic acid and activates the Psal promoter to drive reporter expression, while the <em>nah</em> gene cluster catalyzes naphthalene-to-salicylate conversion.
  </p>

  <p data-text-en="However, after being transferred into E. coli DH5α, the native system showed severe limitations. The wild-type Psal-Pr bidirectional promoter poorly matches the E. coli transcriptional system, resulting in low transcription efficiency. Native NahR exhibits poor sensitivity to low-concentration salicylic acid. The original degradation promoter is weak and limits naphthalene conversion efficiency. The unoptimized system presents high baseline, low signal output and narrow dynamic range, which cannot detect trace environmental naphthalene pollution. Based on these deficiencies, we carried out multi-round rational engineering and system optimization."
     data-text-zh="然而，将该通路转入大肠杆菌DH5α后，原生系统暴露出明显局限：野生型Psal‑Pr双向启动子与大肠杆菌转录系统适配性差，转录效率低；天然NahR对低浓度水杨酸的敏感性不足；原始降解启动子活性弱，限制了萘的转化效率。未经优化的系统本底高、信号输出弱、动态范围窄，无法检出环境中痕量的萘污染。基于以上缺陷，我们开展了多轮理性设计与系统优化。">
    However, after being transferred into <em>E. coli</em> DH5α, the native system showed severe limitations. The wild-type Psal-Pr bidirectional promoter poorly matches the <em>E. coli</em> transcriptional system, resulting in low transcription efficiency. Native NahR exhibits poor sensitivity to low-concentration salicylic acid. The original degradation promoter is weak and limits naphthalene conversion efficiency. The unoptimized system presents high baseline, low signal output and narrow dynamic range, which cannot detect trace environmental naphthalene pollution. Based on these deficiencies, we carried out multi-round rational engineering and system optimization.
  </p>
</section>

